ly harming  her son I didn't know the game was  written to get him in there to draw him  in there and to keep him in there so  that they could make money  the legend of mir3 stabbing its another  online gaming incident with tragic  real-life ramifications legend of mere  players q Cheng Wei and Zhu K Yan  jointly earned a very rare very virtual  Dragon sabre sword in 2005 but Jue  decided to sell the sword on e-bay  without Q's consent earning around 870  dollars for the sale the two players  couldn't come to a reasonable agreement  as to proper dispersal of payment for  the sword so q stabs you to death in his  sleep q was sentenced to life in prison  but will be eligible for parole in 2020  the FarmVille murder sadly even  farmville can turn evil in the wrong  hands Alexandra Tobias a 22 year old  mother was so addicted to the game that  she shook her three-month-old son to  death because his crying interrupted her  playing  Tobias received a 50-year prison  sentence for her actions in 2011 at one  point she allegedly confessed to a  fellow inmate that she hid her baby's  head against the computer monitor in the  process of trying to shake him into  silence unfortunately it's not all that  uncommon for children to suffer while  parents game the world of warcraft  murder the story of Rebecca colleen  kristy offers a worst case scenario when  it comes to game addiction Kristy spent  such an inordinate amount of time  playing Warcraft that she allowed her  three-year-old daughter to starve to  death  prosecutors found that Kristi had just  engaged in a non-stop 15 hour warcraft  session prior to finally calling 911 who  was found unresponsive she was  subsequently sentenced to 25 years in  prison for the crime of neglect on the  other hand some parents go above and  beyond for their kids as we see next  water intoxication for a Nintendo Wii  in 2007 the Nintendo Wii was still hard  to get in the US so the Sacramento based  radio station KD &amp; E decided to run a  c